# Rename, do not annotate

When a name is wrong, **change the name**. Do not leave the old identifier and add a comment, README note, or alias that says what it “really” means.

This includes TypeScript types and files, component inputs and outputs, CSS class names, and user-facing terms.

## Wrong

Keep `buttonKind` because renaming would touch every template, then write `// this is the visual variant`.

## Right

Rename to `variant` and update the call sites. A wide rename is justified when the identifier is wrong.

Avoiding the edit is not a reason to ship the wrong name.
